        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "98efbd3f-ed4d-5514-81a2-9c75cd13d6b1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: American Scientist, Dwell, Global Open Access Forum\n- Organizations: Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society, National Public Radio\n- People: Lara Hedberg Deam, Karrie Jacobs, James Nestor\n- Places: San Francisco\n- Roles: Editor-in-Chief\n- Topics: science and technology magazines, open access\n\nFacts:\n- American Scientist is an American bimonthly science and technology magazine that has been published since 1913 by Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society.\n- The Global Open Access Forum was created in September 1998 by American Scientist, which is published by Sigma Xi, and it was originally called the September98-Forum.\n- Dwell was launched with a magazine in September 2000 by Lara Hedberg Deam to bridge the gap between design professionals and enthusiasts.\n- Karrie Jacobs was Dwell's Editor-in-Chief at its September 2000 launch.\n- James Nestor is a San Francisco-based journalist who has written for Dwell, National Public Radio, The New York Times, Outside magazine, Men's Journal, and the San Francisco Chronicle magazine.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e3994518-18e5-5729-a7d4-7198f7a92cdc",
        "text": "Page: American Scientist. Sentence: American Scientist (informally abbreviated AmSci) is an American bimonthly science and technology magazine published since 1913 by Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society.\nPage: Dwell (magazine). Sentence: It was launched with a magazine in September 2000 to bridge the gap between design professionals and enthusiasts by Lara Hedberg Deam with architecture and design critic Karrie Jacobs as its Editor-in-Chief.\nPage: Global Open Access Forum. Sentence: It was created by the American Scientist, which is published by Sigma Xi, in September 1998, before the term \"Open Access\" (OA) was coined, and it was originally called the \"September98-Forum.\"\nPage: James Nestor (writer). Sentence: James Nestor is a San Francisco-based journalist who has written for \"Outside magazine\", \"Men's Journal\", \"Dwell\" magazine, National Public Radio, \"The New York Times\", the San Francisco Chronicle magazine, and others.",
